1
00:00:00,601 --> 00:00:01,631
(Leonard:)I worked hard on
that speech, too.

2
00:00:01,636 --> 00:00:03,936
(Penny:)Oh. You could tell it to me.

3
00:00:03,938 --> 00:00:05,668
(Leonard:)Oh, thank you,
but I'm okay.

4
00:00:05,673 --> 00:00:06,973
(Penny:)Are you sure?

5
00:00:06,974 --> 00:00:08,774
(Penny:)I could pretend I'm a
high school cheerleader

6
00:00:08,776 --> 00:00:10,706
(Penny:)who can't control herself
around esteemed alumni.

7
00:00:13,046 --> 00:00:15,046
(Leonard:)Greetings, distinguished
cheerleaders.

8
00:00:15,049 --> 00:00:17,279
Ooh!

9
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:21,055
(Howard:)Okay, the WiFi extender
is on, the camera's on,

10
00:00:21,055 --> 00:00:22,485
(Howard:)they're both on
the same network;

11
00:00:22,490 --> 00:00:23,860
(Howard:)we should be
getting an image.

12
00:00:23,858 --> 00:00:26,128
(Sheldon:)All I see is a black screen.

13
00:00:26,127 --> 00:00:27,727
(Sheldon:)And my own reflection.

14
00:00:29,229 --> 00:00:30,129
(Sheldon:)I look sad.

15
00:00:32,632 --> 00:00:34,232
(Howard:)Maybe we should
recalibrate it.

16
00:00:34,235 --> 00:00:35,905
(Sheldon:)All right.
Step one:

17
00:00:35,903 --> 00:00:37,973
(Howard:)rapidly flip
the calibration switch

18
00:00:37,972 --> 00:00:39,872
(Howard:)from the fully up
to the fully down positions

19
00:00:39,874 --> 00:00:41,704
(Howard:)for at least ten times.

20
00:00:41,709 --> 00:00:44,639
It actually says "at least"?

21
00:00:44,645 --> 00:00:46,145
(Penny:)Yeah.

22
00:00:46,147 --> 00:00:47,847
Why would they say "at least"?

23
00:00:47,848 --> 00:00:49,148
(Sheldon:)Is it ten toggles?

24
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:51,050
Is it 100 toggles? You know?

25
00:00:51,052 --> 00:00:52,922
Is it 1,000 toggles?

26
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,890
10,000 toggles?
100,000 toggles?

27
00:00:54,889 --> 00:00:57,259
Sheldon!

28
00:00:57,258 --> 00:01:00,158
(Sheldon:)You see where
I'm going with this.

